apology-death.md:1: argue/readings: S2 is read 2 ways: apology-death.logic.r2 and apology-death.logic.r2.2 have "nothingness → dreamless_sleep"; apology-death.logic.r2.3 has nothing from it; they differ when only "death is a state of nothingness and utter unconsciousness, a sleep undisturbed even by dreams" is true, which the second allows
apology-death.md:1: argue/answered: S2: answered no, which keeps apology-death.logic.r2 and apology-death.logic.r2.2, to: Suppose "death is a state of nothingness and utter unconsciousness, a sleep undisturbed even by dreams" is true and "death is like a night of sleep undisturbed even by dreams, eternity being then only a single night" is false. Is S2, "Now if you suppose that there is no consciousness, but a sleep like the sleep of him who is undisturbed even by dreams, death will be an unspeakable gain.", true then?
